            {
              "id": "5a927dce-4875-434e-b560-dbe96eeb6296",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>The Rules Are No Game: The Strategy of Communication</strong></em> was written by Anthony Wilden, published by Routledge, January 1, 1987."
            },
            {
              "id": "9f810e52-c932-43e3-a606-f96fc94daae7",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "f4d0662c-fd32-4df4-b31b-8657444cb801",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Literacy is power, but power is never absolute. Like other modes of communication it is moulded by codes or rules; and these constraints - of system, structure, and strategy - are the rules that are no game.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "8dac3f19-8f21-4970-bfd6-e19001b761eb",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            }
